===Vanguards===
{{Main|Vanguard}}
The Vanguards consist of three monsters, one melee, one ranged, and one magic. The melee Vanguard has lots of tentacles flailing out, the ranged Vanguard has only a few tentacles flailing out and others holding rocks, and the magic Vanguard has its tentacles retracted. Each Vanguard is weak to the combat style in the [[combat triangle]] that counters its own.

Each Vanguard's attack consists of three hits. The melee Vanguard directs all three hits at its target, the ranged and magic Vanguards launch three projectiles, but only one is aimed directly at their target. The other two are launched elsewhere, though it is possible to be hit by two or even all three. Protection prayers significantly reduce the accuracy and damage of these attacks.

The Vanguards' health must be kept close together. In groups of five or more, the Vanguard with the most health cannot be more than 33% of its maximum hitpoints ahead of the Vanguard with the least health. This increases to 40% in groups of four or fewer. If the difference is close to the threshold, a dark spiral appears around the Vanguard with the most health, while a light spiral appears around the Vanguard with the least health. If the difference goes past the threshold, all three Vanguards will shuffle and fully heal.

The Vanguards will periodically shuffle around the room, moving either clockwise or counterclockwise. They cannot be targeted while shuffling, though attacks made before they started to move will still land. Players in their path will take 3-6 damage every few ticks. The Vanguards will reemerge once all three are in position. If a fatal hit would land on a Vanguard while they are shuffling, it will instead be left at 1 hitpoint.

In solo encounters, players will usually need to chase whichever Vanguard has the most health. Staying around the edges of the room helps avoid drawing attacks from the others, as being attacked by multiple Vanguards at once can deal a lot of damage. In larger teams, players can generally stay in place and switch gear for whichever Vanguard moves to them after each shuffle.

If a player walks under the ranged Vanguard, it won't move while they're stood under it. This can be used to hide if a player accidentally draws aggro of multiple Vanguards at once.

The Vanguards will all drop specific sets of potions on death; each Vanguard drop one of their respective combat potion. The melee Vanguard will also drop two [[Xeric's aid (+)]], the ranged Vanguard will drop one Xeric's aid, two [[Revitalisation (+)]] and the magic Vanguard will drop one Xeric's aid, one Revitalisation and one [[Prayer enhance (+)]]. One of these three will also guarantee an [[Overload (+)]], though the other two also have a chance to drop it. This makes them very useful for no-prep runs, as the player is not likely to consume a large amount of supplies compared to other bosses while gaining vital potions.

