==Plugins==
*The '''CoX Vanguards''' plugin is useful for figuring out the health of the Vanguards for all encounters, showing their health percentages in groups and how much damage can be done before safely soloing them.
**Additionally, the player can toggle their colors to tell which Vanguard is which, along with showing the wander range of the melee Vanguard.
*'''CoX Thieving''' can allow the player to more easily pinpoint the chests containing bats/poison.
*'''Chambers of Xeric''' can be used to show layout of the raid (although not as efficient as the official client, since it is unable to map unknowns), points gained during the raid and more easily identify ideal and less than ideal rooms in a small/large layout.

